# No Co-Authored-By / AI attribution

Never add AI or tool attribution to git commits or pull requests. This is a hard project rule — not optional.

## Forbidden

- `Co-Authored-By:` / `Co-authored-by:` trailers (Cursor, Claude, Codex, Copilot, or any other)
- "Generated with …", "Made with …", or similar attribution lines in commit messages or PR bodies
- Leaving an injected trailer in place because "the hook added it"

## Required

- Commit and PR text must contain only the human-facing summary of the change
- After every `git commit` / `git commit --amend`, read `git log -1 --format=%B` and confirm there is **no** `Co-authored-by` line
- If a hook, IDE, or tool injects attribution: strip it before finishing
  - Prefer rewriting the local commit message (`commit-tree` + `update-ref`, or equivalent) so the trailer never remains
  - Do **not** use `--no-verify` unless the user explicitly asks
- For **local-only** commits (not pushed to `origin`): if any already contain `Co-authored-by`, rewrite that range and remove the trailer before finishing the task

```text
# ❌ BAD
Prepare Flatpak packaging for Flathub app ID.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# ✅ GOOD
Prepare Flatpak packaging for Flathub app ID.
```
